#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124474 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124285 :question/id #uuid "7c28a136-0b86-5d13-a5f8-b0dd0e0ea1ba" :question/math-academy-id "e-3963" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=|x-2|-2,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\n- $x \\in (-\\infty, 2]$\n\n- $x \\in (0, \\infty)$\n\n- $x \\in (-1,4]$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's graph the given function. The graph of the function $f(x)=|x-2|-2$ can be obtained in the following way:  \n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $2$ units to the right,  to get $y= |x-2|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y= |x-2|$ by $2$ units down to get $f(x)=|x-2|-2.$\n\n![](images/60/60c2601abfd3c4034991408f47b75c8cf70a1bccb72f73b2f9624a52d0ed7b42.png)\n\nNow, remember that a function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the interval $x\\in(-\\infty,2].$  Indeed, on this interval, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/45/45b0cdd26280d9379a449af41edbc9e69dd9d76f3b4116d938fbe708c21f6f29.png)\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on any of the intervals $x\\in(0,\\infty)$ and $x \\in (-1,4].$ On these intervals, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/55/55b8483c59362d3a59dfd269db74f2c5f17a97cee1f25c896ece16890d80bd42.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048598} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049474} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049620} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049716}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125195 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a40ae285-433a-5246-af0a-c88929a17e44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438362} {:answer/id #uuid "e15901cc-60b2-5acb-8bde-29e449df57e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a40ae285-433a-5246-af0a-c88929a17e44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438362} :answer-field/id #uuid "31c00eba-5f85-593e-a961-4f82d5b230c4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439210} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e9d17c6-21e1-5f62-96ed-ad5565cf2dd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438364} {:answer/id #uuid "dffc387b-695d-57a9-8327-5b7f95278dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dffc387b-695d-57a9-8327-5b7f95278dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438365} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8399770-7bd0-5bd4-871d-487953742e13" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439211} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e0e5c91-0cdc-57c0-b0a0-e40824bbc4e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438366} {:answer/id #uuid "0fd86b3d-4e5d-5a86-912e-c80f82634797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fd86b3d-4e5d-5a86-912e-c80f82634797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438367} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fca4c40-e85f-5c68-8f26-936d0e0fe80e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439212}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ea11e93-5fca-5cd0-afe6-c972b9a2cce3" :question/math-academy-id "q-66482" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={x}^{2}+2,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-2,2)$\n- **II.** $x\\in [0,\\infty )$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,0]$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)={x}^{2}+2$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y={x}^{2}.$\n\n- Translate it by $2$ units up to get $f(x)={x}^{2}+2.$\n\n![](images/ff/ff3d1ac7500d83574b8671b23e99d4a0f1dbd6ab9cebc906aa06ff2c21f95345.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-2,2).$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/a7/a71ce036adc5dc0b15fce9e367a0c8512699dc6a7814f4e9a1886696d2abad6e.png)\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the intervals $x\\in [0,\\infty )$ and  $x\\in (-\\infty ,0].$ On these intervals, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/68/6858bd1fab8d9659c84fa941cd63ee9f509c8364dce0e753706c640ecfe6e9ec.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125196 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09a0484c-3bf3-547a-ac9e-662c11c6407f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438424} {:answer/id #uuid "6ab65fa6-d3bc-5f7c-91bd-73caca0fcd95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ab65fa6-d3bc-5f7c-91bd-73caca0fcd95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438425} :answer-field/id #uuid "30028ca6-c29b-51ed-af09-6b88025b44c3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439241} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9b93f81-81c6-593b-a3d8-7d442e66fafb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438426} {:answer/id #uuid "2c402c3a-58a6-59c8-a229-20d0ef1effb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c402c3a-58a6-59c8-a229-20d0ef1effb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438427} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f6bf338-1e4e-5783-b25f-385d42279cae" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439242} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd1cef17-f883-5968-9f40-6254da05ef78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438428} {:answer/id #uuid "019d68a4-3d69-5257-8671-f80deae89182" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "019d68a4-3d69-5257-8671-f80deae89182" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438429} :answer-field/id #uuid "637c2a4f-d4ef-5b97-ae47-4358c0bec58d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439243}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c08528cd-5efd-5572-9af4-e4dc31c682da" :question/math-academy-id "q-66723" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=x+1,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$\n- **II.** $x\\in (-1,\\infty )$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-10,5)$" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $1$ and $y$-intercept $1,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/00/00d6394343d441ee10fa20ee029b8f89b52ff1e6ded8e7fdbe0756118212f1a8.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ it is also invertible on  $x\\in (-1,\\infty )$ and $x\\in (-10,5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234209 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85558fe1-9c94-53cd-9b06-9d10fd915bfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439873} {:answer/id #uuid "41bb42a2-237c-50d2-bde6-1e67a38a37e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41bb42a2-237c-50d2-bde6-1e67a38a37e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439874} :answer-field/id #uuid "c62a73cf-8c33-535d-9dea-0086d3e41c0e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440294} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dffdc7f5-2b92-5cae-91de-71f301a1f0da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439875} {:answer/id #uuid "528273a2-3a9d-5b9a-9b7a-08f3145a6a84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439876}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dffdc7f5-2b92-5cae-91de-71f301a1f0da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439875} :answer-field/id #uuid "18169496-ec76-51fc-b481-2edec3fc6630" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440295} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ce25a91-38a4-5e06-8dbc-24d243e66ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439877} {:answer/id #uuid "1ae5b007-91e6-5976-a3c2-72321bebd9a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ce25a91-38a4-5e06-8dbc-24d243e66ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439877} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5c6a5b6-c726-593a-9362-e5d7e8c23832" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "912ff428-058e-5197-af7a-fcbe7f3d6387" :question/math-academy-id "q-66785" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=|x-4|+2,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,3)$\n- **II.** $x\\in (1,\\infty )$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,5]$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x-4|+2$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $4$ units to the right,  to get $y=|x-4|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=|x-4|$ by $2$ units up to get $f(x)=|x-4|+2.$\n\n![](images/56/56956d0f23ae6828098507712fd00525dc4f114a195716dc16e63d8475e9c143.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,3).$  Indeed, on this interval, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on any of the intervals $x\\in (1,\\infty )$  and $(-\\infty ,5].$ On each of these intervals, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323741 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff35ccf9-01ac-52ac-880d-c4dc02e90a40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438202} {:answer/id #uuid "94989d8f-895b-52e3-984a-8b2b79d456fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94989d8f-895b-52e3-984a-8b2b79d456fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438203} :answer-field/id #uuid "aacdaa79-2d58-50ce-8011-be966bc39789" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439130} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39cdea1e-5a53-54bf-bea0-69611a5b3d3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438204} {:answer/id #uuid "92557738-afb1-50f3-81d0-90a570989d5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39cdea1e-5a53-54bf-bea0-69611a5b3d3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438204} :answer-field/id #uuid "edf49524-0b72-5fcd-b414-ca90461589ed" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439131} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b8cc712-dfda-5034-8c6b-b4e359500cce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438206} {:answer/id #uuid "c3ceb92f-1179-5f20-aac2-a8c21430d24b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3ceb92f-1179-5f20-aac2-a8c21430d24b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438207} :answer-field/id #uuid "496eb34a-e1a6-5d05-95ad-5faa3b236c5b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aef31e6b-2918-5842-b5c4-348781827064" :question/math-academy-id "q-36010" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=|x-2|+1,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n- **II.** $x\\in (1,\\infty )$\n- **III.** $x\\in (2,4]$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x-2|+1$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $2$ units to the right,  to get $y=|x-2|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=|x-2|$ by $1$ unit up to get $f(x)=|x-2|+1.$\n\n![](images/ce/ceab1637313ae53869cc1e59f6a56ad6cb920a83dffba482558b696188df0d36.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$ and $x\\in (2,4].$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/a4/a47169838785b6f4ac78253252bcedc3c2cb752a655feac9945e20dd40563b4f.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (1,\\infty ).$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/14/14ed35294e1179ffd9efaf87fa8ac1eb99853a7da344e462c2cb0dda74c3b78f.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335885 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1d4299d-351a-5fe9-a670-073cc9e5de38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438368} {:answer/id #uuid "fa255a93-20e8-54e8-97be-3ba846492184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa255a93-20e8-54e8-97be-3ba846492184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438369} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f1aeed1-5d5d-55f5-b47f-ad533ff3c9e9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439213} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98321251-a137-534c-9fe9-52d7da6b8d72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438370} {:answer/id #uuid "9af520a8-05f9-5db2-8313-3ee23294d164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9af520a8-05f9-5db2-8313-3ee23294d164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438371} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba5de37a-efe1-5701-9c49-2975bdd66304" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439214} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20ea6006-9ee8-51ed-af73-840f5ecd72e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438372} {:answer/id #uuid "5b63ac11-cd0e-537a-9f3c-14ff4d9d34c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b63ac11-cd0e-537a-9f3c-14ff4d9d34c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438373} :answer-field/id #uuid "938f0d88-c3f0-572a-a97c-94e4a874dfb3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439215}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2712841f-ac1b-5d69-a817-019e60c121da" :question/math-academy-id "q-66483" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=1-x,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$\n- **II.** $x\\in (0,\\infty )$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-2,2)$" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $-1$ and $y$-intercept $1,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/73/73d9277c040ae457ba6d96e162574edbeeef965d181fa6011ca4ab0e4644bd82.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ it is also invertible on $x\\in (0,\\infty )$ and $x\\in (-2,2).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335893 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43d7d582-0e08-5fe3-8e62-df514f329d5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438406} {:answer/id #uuid "41998fef-2e26-54fe-acf9-a5788490ab47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41998fef-2e26-54fe-acf9-a5788490ab47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438407} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0378409-4fc6-5ebd-a16b-b9ce526ffed5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439232} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd89e6d4-4284-5cef-ad54-c1065cbfd742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438408} {:answer/id #uuid "9f2c5391-3de3-59c1-a286-2ed065c30bef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd89e6d4-4284-5cef-ad54-c1065cbfd742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438408} :answer-field/id #uuid "5868dcf2-b093-50db-b08d-7add6f5064eb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439233} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1e919a5-9466-584c-b9bd-7477e3370765" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438410} {:answer/id #uuid "a16d2f7b-c0fb-5e81-8da1-26bc5ef53cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a16d2f7b-c0fb-5e81-8da1-26bc5ef53cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438411} :answer-field/id #uuid "d36afc1b-e6be-563c-8f1f-8a95a433bde4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439234}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26ae354c-e4a4-50d9-b820-8ba146650b10" :question/math-academy-id "q-66669" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=(x-2)^{2},$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (2,\\infty )$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in (-1,5)$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,2]$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=(x-2)^{2},$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n1\\. Take the curve $y={x}^{2}.$\n\n2\\. Translate it by $2$ units  to  the right  $f(x)=(x-2)^{2}.$\n\n![](images/1e/1e3ac550e35a3dc93b3e26e5834f763847b04f5133de02e368124f54dd2b9dd6.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-1,5).$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/3e/3ebb316ca122b6786b8ef501fc7c56f8e0e68c8cfc32e5801c493d38382fc26c.png)\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (2,\\infty )$  and $x\\in (-\\infty ,2].$  On these intervals, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/86/86c7c9cacc7a3868565f33130563ffed0ca423aa087e76cc08d103ea171822ed.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72a9977b-4906-5466-8a2e-080981fbbc3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438412} {:answer/id #uuid "bffb12a2-2512-535f-a05a-93d1ecd5edbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bffb12a2-2512-535f-a05a-93d1ecd5edbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438413} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cb31fe6-c55b-53f4-9367-7623acd76b6c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439235} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb16cbba-9564-553b-b9ec-711aa8dbca6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438414} {:answer/id #uuid "b93a4fce-89ce-58fb-80e2-43edf373bb3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b93a4fce-89ce-58fb-80e2-43edf373bb3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438415} :answer-field/id #uuid "6db6c671-dedf-53e0-be3f-fcd379f0e138" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439236} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b379a802-24be-59ce-b981-52720b5955d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438416} {:answer/id #uuid "c0459670-ed37-5d93-b901-b40e7e54aeca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b379a802-24be-59ce-b981-52720b5955d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438416} :answer-field/id #uuid "ade1d675-9ef4-50ee-b050-c20ae72bdedc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ffb9d3e2-6b9a-5fb3-b64e-0b7d921759d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-66679" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=(x-1)^{2}-2,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in (1,\\infty )$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in (-1,3]$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=(x-1)^{2}-2$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n1\\. Take the curve $y={x}^{2}.$\n\n2\\. Translate it by $1$ units to the right,  to get $y=(x-1)^{2}.$\n\n3\\. Finally, translate $y=(x-1)^{2}$  by $2$ units down to get $f(x)=(x-1)^{2}-2.$\n\n![](images/f5/f53a4f97166877085c90acc01e3f8d0c6ac7bb3f704bbfb792d747122d314013.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$ and $x\\in (1,\\infty ).$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/b0/b088c8ed1974a7c259dd54f85aec7a124579981971babfe8dee0313ca23b6458.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-1,3].$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/b3/b3af13782a01213bb09fdeef38fbeb3fbca3f41348036e6786b4efa74a0166b4.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335901 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ff36d03-5cc0-5d73-83c4-e624a390bbc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438418} {:answer/id #uuid "530329fb-ce87-5e84-b072-5a38f2ebf633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "530329fb-ce87-5e84-b072-5a38f2ebf633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438419} :answer-field/id #uuid "919e5c28-bbf2-5c80-b2d5-d434d820a43f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439238} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d13bb14f-1c20-5e94-8700-4dbd1f20f1b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438420} {:answer/id #uuid "78447fbd-2164-5eac-8c2b-44e4dc612b4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d13bb14f-1c20-5e94-8700-4dbd1f20f1b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438420} :answer-field/id #uuid "358639a5-54d9-573f-8827-054bd466e1e6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439239} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38e632a0-32b1-57b2-ba0b-ca870495c039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438422} {:answer/id #uuid "361ecb6e-6cba-52c2-866f-654d5b3bf821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38e632a0-32b1-57b2-ba0b-ca870495c039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438422} :answer-field/id #uuid "02fe17af-c7ed-530c-9d35-2b5a79dc67c3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1120070d-b929-5ac5-a6ba-244a40b57b70" :question/math-academy-id "q-66687" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=-{x}^{2}+1,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,0]$\n- **II.** $x\\in (-2,2]$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-2,\\infty )$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=-{x}^{2}+1$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y={x}^{2}.$\n\n- Reflect its graph across  the $x$-axis to get $y=-{x}^{2}.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=-{x}^{2}$  by $1$ unit up to  get $f(x)=-{x}^{2}+1.$\n\n![](images/83/83a9f5966c76b89b2cad9c6244e2e447fb0052fc7f946df954df76265628c4a7.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n*The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,0].$ On this interval, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/f6/f694b6b1bc979289b748758385e05575990bd866457e75a84fbf7bdf335c03b9.png)\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-2,2].$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once. Since  $(-2,2]$ is a subset of $(-2,\\infty )$, our function is not invertible on $x\\in (-2,\\infty )$ either.\n\n![](images/c0/c03118f3fd0193910b49e26ab5ea56e4320fd23583feb3267cd4442d0a157583.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335903 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cefd8d5e-1289-5ad1-914c-ab2775321488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438436} {:answer/id #uuid "b576a8c1-7ea3-5fa1-8acc-832863849d14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b576a8c1-7ea3-5fa1-8acc-832863849d14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438437} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ca5f16c-d2d5-56cb-9b50-6ad3cade9608" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439247} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "befc7759-bd31-5c8e-9555-3cb0dd101a77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438438} {:answer/id #uuid "43259996-4978-511c-985e-68d25446c510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43259996-4978-511c-985e-68d25446c510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438439} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6c11a88-ed6a-52c6-9f46-d560f8833eee" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439248} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43a190ae-1ab7-5e97-aea2-ab2e9632fae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438440} {:answer/id #uuid "18ea5186-8355-5092-9c9e-79cb796117a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18ea5186-8355-5092-9c9e-79cb796117a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438441} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a5a0d91-6853-5fb1-88df-fb42944cb144" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02e022db-b323-5e31-af64-39f79b6a6465" :question/math-academy-id "q-66725" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=-x+3,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in (0.5,\\infty )$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in [-3,\\sqrt{2}]$" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $-1$ and $y$-intercept $3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/aa/aaa05d1ab0fd630dacd81723fe00472cb901fb6f73af5f111f44459476191c0f.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ it is also invertible on  $x\\in (0.5,\\infty )$ and $x\\in [-3,\\sqrt{2}].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335904 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc2ebd76-b3da-51ec-9bb6-c0a8d8726a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438442} {:answer/id #uuid "ed90097f-008e-5903-8afb-166e0fb732b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed90097f-008e-5903-8afb-166e0fb732b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438443} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb140f0c-688c-52f8-a90f-9018b950a280" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439250} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efd9c021-33f1-5537-af5a-c438ea2991ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438444} {:answer/id #uuid "4d46b3e2-aa3f-52ac-bda8-6b775f310423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d46b3e2-aa3f-52ac-bda8-6b775f310423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438445} :answer-field/id #uuid "5614c87c-6ed3-55e6-95b6-98e904f5c5d1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439251} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73ccc799-d970-5891-a63d-3482846a277e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438446} {:answer/id #uuid "52ff3f43-d7ba-5b03-a6cf-148b6c9c461e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73ccc799-d970-5891-a63d-3482846a277e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438446} :answer-field/id #uuid "404e5779-63f4-5bb6-b2a6-acf55f92288b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439252}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0ee60b09-63e9-5076-abae-7337fc233de5" :question/math-academy-id "q-66729" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=|x-1|-2,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in (1,\\infty )$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,2]$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x-1|-2$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n1\\. Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n2\\. Translate it by $1$ units to the right,  to get $y=|x-1|.$\n\n3\\. Finally, translate $y=|x-1|$ by $2$ units down to get $f(x)=|x-1|-2.$\n\n![](images/75/753840da17642582f9dbc0debc18f1fa3efcbbb11142894c1dd823ad6c0c630a.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$ and $x\\in (1,\\infty ).$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/15/15f1c797cbddd2ac8e2e9c5be72f842e7d1accfc5f619af57b1f35a27e1015c0.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,2].$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/a1/a100489b49da7b06c98783b1b1c4ec0de9d891fc2b22f4b36b1a0ac2d54fc4f3.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  and II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335906 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e58af68f-eae1-53c6-9223-c7c0080b2c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438448} {:answer/id #uuid "5371e2e8-a318-5761-84cf-2a344ab71943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438449}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e58af68f-eae1-53c6-9223-c7c0080b2c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438448} :answer-field/id #uuid "1aab5ce5-7c11-54ef-9873-01b2782d09cb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439253} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af8f6888-4ad1-59e7-bb89-aa5f77d9746f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438450} {:answer/id #uuid "aeb5ab9d-c02f-5f8d-ae8c-1482c9a4f08b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aeb5ab9d-c02f-5f8d-ae8c-1482c9a4f08b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438451} :answer-field/id #uuid "5211022b-a915-5d40-8743-afe759a8dd9a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439254} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64cbf680-9981-52b0-97b5-fea787285feb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438452} {:answer/id #uuid "557bf5d6-ae71-5f3d-acc6-c84051652a1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "557bf5d6-ae71-5f3d-acc6-c84051652a1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438453} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac161744-e926-5973-8bfb-6bbc90ec7d60" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7aa0547e-3ef1-575a-ba36-cf93ffa1c8dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-66778" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=|x+1|-3,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n- **II.** $x\\in [1,\\infty )$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x+1|-3$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $1$ units to the left,  to get $y=|x+1|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=|x+1|$ by $3$ units down to get $f(x)=|x+1|-3.$\n\n![](images/3b/3b9f56280089991c7db7652d84a777edd5c5e012921f0d48362f4fc3e4fd2a6e.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]$ and $x\\in [1,\\infty ).$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/fd/fd0b0fe70e009f43e80b0f712b6cfd576deb4c4c0457f61adae04cf7e44f140c.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,1].$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/58/582ec1960b053731bf201c84d8c58fd4e1734a2b085cd5549a01aace4b600b4a.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396687 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76dd5d19-bff7-5270-8dec-36984c572a42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438430} {:answer/id #uuid "82576145-5d09-54e1-b8ab-117f2f475ddd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82576145-5d09-54e1-b8ab-117f2f475ddd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438431} :answer-field/id #uuid "12cd27e7-f491-592d-bc1c-bffcd308ed10" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439244} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f15d1f4c-40fe-57bc-b297-88961d557422" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438432} {:answer/id #uuid "e8d21173-1383-59eb-8cfe-f2c8b7016e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8d21173-1383-59eb-8cfe-f2c8b7016e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438433} :answer-field/id #uuid "edd44f0e-e428-5211-9041-ee63c8f7fcd9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fdc3a0d-226e-5b29-bf47-7e99b81a72d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438434} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd56e5c-f931-59ed-ae20-782cc1018117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cd56e5c-f931-59ed-ae20-782cc1018117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438435} :answer-field/id #uuid "786df526-ba10-57de-ad81-45417b5eaddb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8061fba9-94fb-59ab-bb67-c981e34d25e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-66724" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=2x+4,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$\n- **II.** $x\\in (10,\\infty )$\n- **III.** $x\\in [-5,5)$" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $2$ and $y$-intercept $4,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/d3/d33314230419ec762bc4ad8603b2e6c3436461cd6b4b6fe4783d12a23d01b660.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ it is also invertible on  $x\\in (10,\\infty )$ and $x\\in [-5,5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"}]}
